{"architectures":["x64","x86"],"id":"alagrede.znote","latestVersion":"4.10.0","media":{"icons":[{"mimeType":"image/png","path":"media/icon.3f3ea39d.png","priority":1,"sha256":"3f3ea39d7e187679cd4d455eddd20ebc5fe607a301c00122c1cf64d9d6494962","source":"winget-legacy"}],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"Markdown-based note-taking app for developers","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"FAQ","DocumentUrl":"https://znote.io/faq.html"}],"license":"Freeware","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"Markdown-based note-taking app for developers","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"FAQ","DocumentUrl":"https://znote.io/faq.html"}],"license":"Freeware","locale":"en-US","name":"znote","packageUrl":"https://github.com/alagrede/znote-app","publisher":"alagrede","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/alagrede/znote-app/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/alagrede","releaseNotes":"Znote 4.10.0\n\n✨ New look\nNew style redesign of the whole app: dark theme, Settings and every dialog, tree view, note list, outline, toolbars with new line icons, AI bar, recorder and command palettes. Lists now show a single highlight, and the Material ripple is gone.\n\n🚀 Features\n- Read-only mode and Live edit / Source toggle in the toolbar. In read mode, copying gives plain text and the AI bar is hidden.\n- No more footer. Help, Settings and Account move to the vault bar, and the AI model picker moves into the Ask AI bar.\n- NPM, Plugins, Functions and MCP are now tabs of Settings and no longer sit in the left bar.\n- Quick search (Cmd/Ctrl+T) works again, as a keyboard-driven palette with recent notes and full-text results.\n- Paste any file. PDFs and documents copied from the Finder or Explorer go into the vault's attachments folder with a [[link]] that opens them in the default app. On macOS, several files can be pasted at once.\n- Show all file types: a new per-vault option that lists every file of the vault in the tree view.\n- Focus mode: a button switches between the readable line length and full width for the focus session only.\n\n🐛 Fixes\n- PowerShell scripts are exported as .ps1.\n- The organization sign-in dialog is now in English and shows login errors inline.","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/alagrede/znote-app/releases/tag/v4.10.0","tags":["dev","editor","electron","markdown","react","znote"]}},"name":"znote","packageUrl":"https://github.com/alagrede/znote-app","publisher":"alagrede","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/alagrede/znote-app/issues","publisherUrl":"https://github.com/alagrede","releaseNotes":"Znote 4.10.0\n\n✨ New look\nNew style redesign of the whole app: dark theme, Settings and every dialog, tree view, note list, outline, toolbars with new line icons, AI bar, recorder and command palettes. Lists now show a single highlight, and the Material ripple is gone.\n\n🚀 Features\n- Read-only mode and Live edit / Source toggle in the toolbar. In read mode, copying gives plain text and the AI bar is hidden.\n- No more footer. Help, Settings and Account move to the vault bar, and the AI model picker moves into the Ask AI bar.\n- NPM, Plugins, Functions and MCP are now tabs of Settings and no longer sit in the left bar.\n- Quick search (Cmd/Ctrl+T) works again, as a keyboard-driven palette with recent notes and full-text results.\n- Paste any file. PDFs and documents copied from the Finder or Explorer go into the vault's attachments folder with a [[link]] that opens them in the default app. On macOS, several files can be pasted at once.\n- Show all file types: a new per-vault option that lists every file of the vault in the tree view.\n- Focus mode: a button switches between the readable line length and full width for the focus session only.\n\n🐛 Fixes\n- PowerShell scripts are exported as .ps1.\n- The organization sign-in dialog is now in English and shows login errors inline.","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/alagrede/znote-app/releases/tag/v4.10.0","tags":["dev","editor","electron","mar